WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.175
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.175 --> 00:02.468
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION, BINGE
DRINKING, SHAMEFUL ACTS NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:02.468 --> 00:03.761
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:03.761 --> 00:04.970
DUE TO RECENT COMPLIANCE ISSUES, THE
BLACK DOT SIZE HAS BEEN INCREASED BY 5%.

00:09.585 --> 00:11.560
A layover in Guam?

00:12.061 --> 00:12.686
Yeah.

00:13.179 --> 00:16.398
So that means we'll be
setting foot in America, right?

00:16.968 --> 00:19.735
Don't get busted for
their obscenity laws, Kouhei.

00:19.735 --> 00:22.029
I hear they're pretty strict over there.

00:24.782 --> 00:26.825
Let me see that bag.

00:26.825 --> 00:28.827
What are you planning to bring?

00:33.749 --> 00:36.544
Better this than
having it confiscated, right?

00:36.544 --> 00:38.921
Good thing we caught this
before leaving.

00:38.921 --> 00:41.257
I don't want any more trouble.

00:42.591 --> 00:43.968
Speaking of which,

00:43.968 --> 00:47.179
even if you see porn in Guam,
you wouldn't buy it, right?

00:47.388 --> 00:48.722
Of course not.

00:51.392 --> 00:52.726
Hand it over.

00:52.726 --> 00:54.270
I knew it.

00:58.809 --> 01:00.310
PALAU

01:07.491 --> 01:09.785
We're finally here.

01:09.785 --> 01:11.245
Is it this late already?

01:12.997 --> 01:15.791
Because the layover in Guam
took quite a bit of time.

01:16.125 --> 01:18.711
What should we do now?

01:18.711 --> 01:21.547
Looks like someone is coming to pick us up.

01:21.742 --> 01:22.798
Is that the one?

01:22.965 --> 01:24.967
DOLPHIN

01:25.342 --> 01:28.637
Anyway, a lot has happened this summer.

01:28.637 --> 01:29.179
Yeah.

01:29.346 --> 01:32.057
Camping on a deserted island
with Kaya-sama.

01:32.057 --> 01:33.851
And going to Iori's place too.

01:33.851 --> 01:36.437
Those weirdos were a real masterpiece.

01:36.645 --> 01:38.731
The hot springs were great, too.

01:39.773 --> 01:41.900
Sounds like fun, doesn't it?

01:41.900 --> 01:42.985
Oh, hello.

01:43.319 --> 01:45.904
It wasn't really a big deal.

01:45.904 --> 01:48.657
No, it sounds like a lot of fun.

01:48.657 --> 01:49.366
Huh?

01:52.286 --> 01:55.748
Especially the parts
when I wasn't there.

01:56.582 --> 01:59.460
C-Cakey?!

02:11.096 --> 02:13.557
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

02:13.557 --> 02:16.769
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3To a city far away, what do you say?

02:16.769 --> 02:19.188
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

02:19.188 --> 02:22.733
To a city far away, what do you say?

02:26.820 --> 02:28.697
Wait a sec, another heatwave?

02:28.697 --> 02:30.407
Temperatures are rising... Huh?!

02:30.407 --> 02:33.619
Our original plans are
totally busted, what now?

02:33.619 --> 02:36.455
But honestly, I'm getting so hyped

02:36.455 --> 02:39.124
Alright, let's roll up
our sleeves and dive in

02:39.124 --> 02:40.918
Rub your sleepy eyes and jump up

02:40.918 --> 02:42.336
Grab the usual shades

02:42.336 --> 02:45.255
Check your gear: Iced coffee, thermos

02:45.255 --> 02:47.925
Clear blue skies, just a trick of summer

02:47.925 --> 02:51.053
The booming speakers
keep calling my name

02:51.387 --> 02:53.889
Even now, I still believe

02:56.809 --> 02:58.769
In unexpected encounters

02:58.769 --> 03:01.355
And the miracles of this season

03:01.355 --> 03:04.608
Summer brings
those swing swing emotions

03:04.608 --> 03:07.361
Ah, even if I get a little carried away

03:07.361 --> 03:12.574
On my mind,
I've only been searching for you

03:12.574 --> 03:18.497
Let the south wind blow you here,
just as you are

03:18.497 --> 03:23.210
Under the blue sky, hold me tight

03:24.044 --> 03:29.466
I want to dream
a summer dream with you

03:30.467 --> 03:32.386
Why is Cakey here?

03:32.386 --> 03:33.971
Aren't you back in your hometown?

03:33.971 --> 03:36.306
I was there until recently.

03:36.306 --> 03:39.268
Day after day,
helping out with farm work.

03:39.810 --> 03:42.104
Thinking back,
those were truly harsh days.

03:42.563 --> 03:44.773
Work faster!

03:45.399 --> 03:47.609
Exhausting manual labor.

03:48.402 --> 03:51.947
But the seniors seemed busy
with job hunting too.

03:52.281 --> 03:54.450
Everyone must be working so hard...

03:54.533 --> 03:56.535
IORI: SUDDEN PLANS FOR DESERT ISLAND
CAMPING. RECRUITING COMPANIONS!

03:56.618 --> 03:57.745
Grandpa.

03:57.870 --> 03:58.787
What is it?

03:58.787 --> 04:01.457
I can't work anymore today.

04:02.499 --> 04:03.959
Why not?

04:04.184 --> 04:04.685
THE NEXT DAY

04:04.710 --> 04:07.296
We have to make up for
yesterday's delays!

04:07.504 --> 04:09.089
Iori and the others might be...

04:09.089 --> 04:10.257
CHEERS
enjoying their youth

04:10.257 --> 04:11.467
CHEERS
on a deserted island.

04:11.759 --> 04:14.720
But well,
it's just the usual members in the end.

04:14.720 --> 04:16.138
Nothing to worry about...

04:16.805 --> 04:18.807
AZUSA: UNEXPECTED ENCOUNTER
ON A DESERT ISLAND!

04:18.974 --> 04:21.643
That bitch is a no-go!

04:22.144 --> 04:23.771
DANGER - BOTTOMLESS SWAMP
What happened?

04:23.979 --> 04:25.731
Are you okay, Aina?

04:25.898 --> 04:27.274
I'm fine.

04:27.566 --> 04:28.817
More importantly...

04:28.817 --> 04:31.904
More crucially, a disaster
had happened to my youth!

04:31.904 --> 04:32.738
A crisis is happeningright in front of us!

04:32.738 --> 04:34.823
AZUSA: UNEXPECTED ENCOUNTER
ON A DESERT ISLAND!

04:34.823 --> 04:38.160
How can you focus on work
when you're glued to this!?

04:38.160 --> 04:40.037
Ah, my phone!

04:40.287 --> 04:42.247
It was absolute hell!

04:43.457 --> 04:46.210
I don't really get it,
but it sounds like you had it rough.

04:46.293 --> 04:49.087
And when I finally got my phone back,

04:49.087 --> 04:52.341
you were having a takoyaki party,
and even went to Iori's place!

04:52.466 --> 04:54.259
You got your phone confiscated?

04:54.259 --> 04:56.345
No wonder we couldn't reach you.

04:56.637 --> 04:59.473
In the end, what's the deal
with this Palau trip!?

04:59.890 --> 05:04.520
I told you guys not to make
fun memories without me!

05:05.312 --> 05:06.480
What fun memories?

05:06.647 --> 05:09.024
More like grueling hell.

05:09.691 --> 05:11.568
Aina, when did you get here?

05:11.568 --> 05:13.821
Right before yesterday,
transiting in Taipei.

05:14.112 --> 05:16.490
Then what about the part-time job here?

05:16.490 --> 05:18.867
Cakey, more importantly...

05:18.867 --> 05:20.369
I have a thing to ask you, too.

05:20.369 --> 05:21.745
Ah, wait a minute.

05:23.914 --> 05:25.791
Let's start moving for now.

05:28.627 --> 05:31.296
This is John, a Dolphin staff member.

05:31.296 --> 05:32.339
Hello.

05:34.508 --> 05:36.260
He understands Japanese, huh?

05:36.260 --> 05:38.178
I was surprised too.

05:38.178 --> 05:40.514
I only understand a little Japanese.

05:40.764 --> 05:42.391
Hey, Kouhei.

05:42.391 --> 05:43.725
What is it, Kitahara?

05:43.725 --> 05:45.978
It's been a while
since we saw Cakey, right?

05:45.978 --> 05:47.187
Yeah.

05:47.187 --> 05:49.398
Wonder what happened over there.

05:49.398 --> 05:50.190
Yeah...

05:50.607 --> 05:51.859
I'm really curious.

05:54.069 --> 05:56.280
- Super curious.
- Super curious.

05:56.446 --> 05:57.739
You try asking.

05:57.739 --> 05:59.783
No no, that's your job.

05:59.783 --> 06:01.660
Maybe she's waiting for a straight man?

06:01.660 --> 06:03.412
Highly possible.

06:04.663 --> 06:07.875
What is it? Staring at my chestright after we meet?

06:08.041 --> 06:09.459
Could it be...

06:10.335 --> 06:12.379
you guys are curious?

06:13.463 --> 06:15.257
If she puts it like that...

06:15.257 --> 06:17.259
it just pisses me off.

06:17.718 --> 06:19.720
Well, let's just ignore it.

06:19.720 --> 06:21.805
Yeah, just ignore it...

06:24.641 --> 06:26.310
- It's crooked!
- It's crooked!

06:26.310 --> 06:27.978
If you're gonna pad it,
do it properly!

06:27.978 --> 06:29.897
Such a sloppy job!

06:30.397 --> 06:32.316
At this point, we must rely on Kotegawa.

06:32.316 --> 06:35.110
Yeah, it's best if she asks.

06:35.736 --> 06:38.906
I heard Japanese is
pretty common in Palau.

06:38.906 --> 06:40.490
People still speak it here.

06:40.782 --> 06:43.911
Phrases like "mata ashita" (see you
tomorrow) or "samui ne" (it's cold).

06:44.703 --> 06:47.956
I heard "cheers" (kanpai) is taken to
mean "tsukare naosu" (let's unwind).

06:47.956 --> 06:49.917
Oh, really?

06:50.000 --> 06:51.960
We do say "tsukare naosu."

06:52.753 --> 06:54.087
Also...

06:54.087 --> 06:56.590
bras are called "boob bands"
(chichi-bando), for example.

06:57.341 --> 06:58.550
- Nice.
- Nice.

06:58.550 --> 07:00.510
You noticed too, Chisa?

07:00.510 --> 07:02.346
What a brilliant guidance!

07:05.974 --> 07:07.517
I see.

07:08.268 --> 07:10.187
She acted like nothing happened.

07:10.187 --> 07:12.105
Such mental fortitude.

07:12.189 --> 07:14.608
But why use that thing all of a sudden?

07:14.608 --> 07:15.692
Beats me.

07:17.027 --> 07:18.654
Aina, is this it?

07:19.071 --> 07:21.907
Yeah, our temporary dorm.

07:21.907 --> 07:24.576
The dorm for the new shop
isn't finished yet.

07:24.576 --> 07:25.577
Really?

07:25.577 --> 07:26.828
Awesome.

07:26.995 --> 07:28.830
So this is the living room.

07:28.830 --> 07:30.415
Whoa.

07:31.166 --> 07:32.626
Looks like a share house.

07:32.626 --> 07:33.710
It even has a loft.

07:33.752 --> 07:34.294
Right.

07:34.294 --> 07:37.297
Shared living room,
but separate bedrooms.

07:37.547 --> 07:38.507
I see.

07:38.590 --> 07:41.385
Like that rental villa back in Okinawa?

07:41.593 --> 07:44.221
- Does it have a pool?
- Or a home theater?

07:44.221 --> 07:46.306
Don't just go wandering around!

07:47.015 --> 07:48.517
Don't worry, Cakey.

07:48.517 --> 07:50.394
We won't open
the room you're using.

07:50.394 --> 07:51.937
Oh...

07:52.604 --> 07:53.647
Oh...

07:54.856 --> 07:55.899
Cakey?

07:55.899 --> 07:57.401
Well...

07:57.651 --> 08:01.363
I thought I'd whip up something
while waiting for you guys.

08:01.363 --> 08:02.656
But it kind of failed.

08:02.656 --> 08:04.074
- Good job!
- Good job!

08:05.909 --> 08:08.662
You bought those for us, right?

08:08.662 --> 08:10.288
How thoughtful of you.

08:10.288 --> 08:11.415
Ah, yeah.

08:11.581 --> 08:13.750
I figured you'd want a drink
when you arrive.

08:15.252 --> 08:17.004
That's Cakey for you.

08:17.004 --> 08:19.172
You know us so well.

08:19.423 --> 08:19.923
Yeah.

08:20.257 --> 08:21.800
But the kitchen is a bit...

08:21.800 --> 08:24.928
- Actually, not just a bit...
- We know your cooking skills all too well.

08:24.928 --> 08:26.805
This is way better.

08:26.805 --> 08:28.432
That's our Cakey.

08:28.432 --> 08:30.350
Still as rude as ever.

08:30.517 --> 08:31.977
Come on, let's drink up.

08:31.977 --> 08:32.728
Hell yeah!

08:33.687 --> 08:34.813
What's wrong?

08:34.813 --> 08:36.773
Nothing, just the usual.

08:36.773 --> 08:37.399
Oh?

08:38.316 --> 08:39.401
Seriously.

08:39.985 --> 08:42.070
I'm glad you could come along.

08:49.036 --> 08:50.537
Well then, welcome to Palau and...

08:50.537 --> 08:52.247
Great to see Cakey again!

08:52.247 --> 08:53.915
Cheers!

08:57.586 --> 08:59.588
The beer here is great too.

08:59.588 --> 09:02.466
Drinking beer on a southern island
is the absolute best.

09:02.466 --> 09:04.426
You guys drink no matter where you are.

09:05.802 --> 09:08.096
So what are we doing tomorrow?

09:08.305 --> 09:10.807
They said to be at the shop by 6.

09:10.807 --> 09:12.267
That's early.

09:12.350 --> 09:14.269
Is the shop near here?

09:14.269 --> 09:16.188
Yeah, about a 5-minute walk.

09:16.354 --> 09:17.689
But I'm a bit worried.

09:17.689 --> 09:18.315
Huh?

09:18.315 --> 09:19.149
About what?

09:19.149 --> 09:21.735
I'm pretty unsure
because I usually oversleep.

09:21.902 --> 09:23.487
Come to think of it, you do.

09:23.487 --> 09:26.114
I probably won't be able to
get up tomorrow either.

09:26.114 --> 09:28.867
Same for me. Just getting here
completely wiped me out.

09:29.576 --> 09:32.287
Well, tomorrow is our first day
working part-time.

09:32.287 --> 09:35.457
Yeah, we should sleep early
so we absolutely won't be late.

09:35.457 --> 09:36.333
Exactly.

09:46.885 --> 09:48.512
The worst possible morning.

09:51.223 --> 09:53.975
Back in the day,
the seniors taught me this.

09:54.309 --> 09:57.521
If you just sleep at the meeting spot,
you wouldn't be late.

09:57.521 --> 10:00.065
What kind of brain-dead logic is that?

10:00.190 --> 10:01.775
Hurry up and clean this up!

10:01.775 --> 10:04.027
Do we need clothes
on a southern island?

10:04.069 --> 10:06.655
You should at least
wear them on the first day.

10:06.655 --> 10:09.074
Wear them until the very last day!

10:09.199 --> 10:11.910
Enough already, hurry up, hurry up!

10:11.910 --> 10:13.787
Stand up! What are you doing?

10:13.787 --> 10:15.497
Wake up!

10:15.497 --> 10:18.166
If we don't hurry, we'll be late, damn it!

10:18.875 --> 10:21.086
It was a long trip, you guys must be tired.

10:21.086 --> 10:22.295
Boss?

10:22.295 --> 10:23.547
Good morning.

10:23.713 --> 10:25.715
- Good morning.
- Yeah, good morning.

10:25.715 --> 10:26.758
Here you go.

10:26.758 --> 10:28.927
Thanks for coming all this way, Iori.

10:28.927 --> 10:29.845
Have some candy.

10:30.095 --> 10:31.096
Thank you.

10:32.848 --> 10:34.307
You know her?

10:34.307 --> 10:36.434
Yeah, didn't I tell you?

10:36.768 --> 10:38.937
Long time no see, Chisa.

10:39.855 --> 10:41.064
Long time no see.

10:43.400 --> 10:44.526
Mom.

10:44.526 --> 10:46.027
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3

10:47.195 --> 10:48.238
Is she...

10:48.238 --> 10:49.489
Kotegawa's mom?

10:49.489 --> 10:50.407
Yeah.

10:51.116 --> 10:53.118
Cakey, you didn't know either?

10:53.118 --> 10:54.661
You met her before we did.

10:54.786 --> 10:56.913
Yeah, but no one told me.

10:56.913 --> 10:58.373
They don't look that similar.

10:59.040 --> 10:59.916
You think?

10:59.916 --> 11:01.418
Their eyes look alike.

11:02.043 --> 11:04.129
Does Nanaka-san take
after the boss more?

11:04.129 --> 11:06.047
I think so.

11:06.756 --> 11:09.009
Let me introduce you to the staff.
Follow me.

11:10.343 --> 11:12.387
It's been a while
since those two met, huh?

11:12.387 --> 11:13.847
It does seem like it.

11:13.847 --> 11:15.307
They look a bit cold...

11:15.307 --> 11:16.433
Yeah.

11:16.975 --> 11:19.436
Well, that's just her personality.

11:19.477 --> 11:22.355
What are you dawdling for?
I hate slowpokes.

11:22.355 --> 11:24.149
Ah, sorry.

11:28.862 --> 11:30.447
We can't wait to work with you.

11:30.447 --> 11:31.364
Nice to meet you.

11:31.364 --> 11:32.407
Nice to meet you.

11:33.158 --> 11:35.285
Maki will explain the job.

11:36.161 --> 11:38.580
I'm Maki, a new guide!

11:38.872 --> 11:39.873
TO-DO LIST: SHOP DISPLAY - DONE
You've heard

11:39.873 --> 11:42.375
TO-DO LIST: SHOP DISPLAY - DONE
this is a new shop about to open, right?

11:42.500 --> 11:43.376
- Yes.
- Yes.

11:43.585 --> 11:44.252
CUSTOMER SERVICE SIMULATION
NOT DONE

11:44.252 --> 11:47.047
so we'll be doing a final dress
rehearsal before opening.

11:47.589 --> 11:50.717
I want you guys to roleplay
as troublesome customers.

11:50.759 --> 11:53.220
It's also to test
the staff's problem-solving skills.

11:54.888 --> 11:57.098
I heard from Manager Kotegawa.

11:57.224 --> 11:59.851
You guys got your
Open Water certifications, right?

12:00.143 --> 12:01.937
Yes, that's right.

12:02.145 --> 12:05.106
And you're also lacking in
basic human decency,

12:05.106 --> 12:06.066
is that true?

12:06.107 --> 12:08.026
- Ha, ha, ha.
- That damn old man!

12:08.401 --> 12:12.489
We just meant to hire some gofers,
we didn't expect to hit the jackpot.

12:12.489 --> 12:15.283
We're lucky to get
capable people like you.

12:15.283 --> 12:16.910
- No, no, no.
- No, no, no.

12:17.035 --> 12:19.371
The manager exaggerated too much.

12:19.371 --> 12:22.374
Kitahara might be like that,
but I'm normal with common sense.

12:22.832 --> 12:26.419
Actually, I received a photo
from the manager beforehand.

12:26.586 --> 12:29.673
Looking at the photo,
you're really a bunch of weirdos.

12:30.048 --> 12:32.717
- How is this weird?
- How is this weird?

12:32.801 --> 12:35.470
Boss, these two are way
beyond our imagination.

12:35.470 --> 12:37.639
Truly rare talents.

12:38.473 --> 12:41.685
So we'll act as customers.

12:41.685 --> 12:44.104
So just act like we would
when visiting a shop?

12:44.104 --> 12:45.563
Yeah, I'm counting on you.

12:46.481 --> 12:47.190
Chisa.

12:48.566 --> 12:49.985
You handle this side.

12:52.320 --> 12:53.154
Yes.

12:54.072 --> 12:56.574
So what should we do now?

12:56.574 --> 12:57.993
Tough one.

12:57.993 --> 12:59.494
What are you talking about?

12:59.703 --> 13:01.746
Just act normal.

13:03.623 --> 13:06.334
Good morning.

13:06.334 --> 13:07.419
Good morning.

13:07.419 --> 13:09.129
Did you sleep well?

13:09.212 --> 13:10.797
Good morning.

13:11.047 --> 13:11.798
Morning.

13:12.007 --> 13:13.717
Are you tired from the trip?

13:14.384 --> 13:15.885
Good morning!

13:15.885 --> 13:17.345
Good morning.

13:19.723 --> 13:23.018
Hey Maki, don't forget to ask
about the customers' health.

13:23.059 --> 13:25.645
Ah, yes, um...

13:25.854 --> 13:27.897
Are your heads okay?

13:28.857 --> 13:30.275
What kind of greeting is that?

13:30.317 --> 13:33.194
Why panic the moment
you see the customers' faces?

13:33.194 --> 13:34.029
I'm so sorry.

13:34.029 --> 13:35.989
Her makeup is as gaudy as a Rakshasa.

13:36.072 --> 13:37.991
I see, so we just act normal, huh?

13:37.991 --> 13:39.784
You were right.

13:39.784 --> 13:42.454
This is not my normal self!

13:42.579 --> 13:42.704
COURSES TAKEN Then, please check these liability waivers.

13:42.704 --> 13:46.291
COURSES TAKEN Then, please check these liability waivers.
READ CAREFULLY BEFORE SIGNING

13:46.291 --> 13:46.875
READ CAREFULLY BEFORE SIGNING

13:46.916 --> 13:49.794
Next, let's try some of the
problematic stuff in here.

13:49.794 --> 13:50.962
What should we do?

13:51.129 --> 13:52.297
Is there a problem?

13:52.339 --> 13:52.505
FAINTED? / MOTION SICKNESS? CAN'T DO HIGH-INTENSITY EXERCISE?

13:52.505 --> 13:57.344
FAINTED? / MOTION SICKNESS? CAN'T DO HIGH-INTENSITY EXERCISE?
There's this part in the checklist, I get really bad motion sickness.

13:57.344 --> 13:57.385
FAINTED? / MOTION SICKNESS? CAN'T DO HIGH-INTENSITY EXERCISE?

13:57.719 --> 13:59.137
Oh, is that so?

13:59.137 --> 14:01.264
We can prepare
countermeasures for you.

14:01.348 --> 14:03.350
The manager is amazing,
not fazed at all.

14:03.350 --> 14:04.559
I see.

14:04.559 --> 14:06.311
Let's play that card too.

14:06.561 --> 14:11.816
Excuse me, I actually have asthma,
whenever I see Lalako-tan my chest gets...

14:11.858 --> 14:14.444
How often do these symptoms occur?

14:14.444 --> 14:15.403
Lalako-tan!

14:15.403 --> 14:16.863
- Sorry.
- What is it?

14:17.072 --> 14:19.574
Actually, I'm pregnant.

14:20.367 --> 14:22.619
You're panicking over
the customer again.

14:22.619 --> 14:24.204
B-Because...

14:24.579 --> 14:26.289
Why are you suddenly pregnant?

14:26.289 --> 14:28.416
Because that's
the first item that I like.

14:28.416 --> 14:30.001
Can't be helped then.

14:31.836 --> 14:34.255
You guys will be renting wetsuits,
right?

14:34.255 --> 14:35.048
Yes.

14:35.048 --> 14:37.175
Then I'll check your sizes.

14:37.509 --> 14:39.344
You'll take a size L, right?

14:39.344 --> 14:40.011
Yes.

14:40.512 --> 14:42.097
Size LL, right?

14:42.222 --> 14:42.806
Yes.

14:43.390 --> 14:45.725
Yoshihara-san, you're a size M, right?

14:45.892 --> 14:47.143
Understood.

14:49.646 --> 14:52.315
Well, looks like everyone is all set.

14:58.655 --> 15:01.116
Maki, that's against the rules.

15:01.199 --> 15:03.743
This is something that could
happen in reality.

15:03.910 --> 15:04.911
I'm sorry.

15:06.913 --> 15:09.124
Then Chisa, give her a hand.

15:10.083 --> 15:12.043
Um, give her a subtle hint...

15:12.043 --> 15:13.837
Stop dilly-dallying.

15:14.003 --> 15:14.671
Manager.

15:15.171 --> 15:16.214
Yes.

15:17.799 --> 15:19.467
Your padding is crooked.

15:19.467 --> 15:19.926
Oops.

15:20.593 --> 15:21.970
Thank you.

15:21.970 --> 15:22.887
You're welcome.

15:23.054 --> 15:25.181
So awesome, as expected of the manager.

15:25.723 --> 15:28.101
You're so useless.

15:28.476 --> 15:32.355
But letting her realize it subtly
is also a way to handle it.

15:32.355 --> 15:33.606
Wrong.

15:33.815 --> 15:36.192
You don't get
customer psychology at all.

15:37.610 --> 15:40.238
Why do you think she padded her chest?

15:40.363 --> 15:42.657
- Well...
- That's...

15:44.451 --> 15:47.579
Because there's someone of
the opposite sex she's into who's here.

15:51.332 --> 15:55.295
That's why we have to warn her
before that person finds out.

15:55.336 --> 15:58.006
Same-sex staff must remind them
quickly and naturally.

15:58.298 --> 15:59.299
I see.

15:59.424 --> 16:00.800
So that's what it was?

16:00.967 --> 16:05.180
Normally,
girls just understand these things.

16:05.513 --> 16:07.474
You still have a lot to learn.

16:09.058 --> 16:11.728
Keep up that when you're out to the sea,
I'm counting on you.

16:11.728 --> 16:12.353
Huh?

16:12.687 --> 16:14.314
We get to go diving right away?

16:14.314 --> 16:16.024
On the very first day?

16:16.357 --> 16:18.485
It's exactly because
it's now that you can go.

16:18.485 --> 16:20.737
Once we open,
you'll be swamped with chores.

16:21.237 --> 16:22.697
Thank you!

16:25.533 --> 16:27.243
This boat is so fast.

16:27.243 --> 16:29.078
Is this a speedboat?

16:29.078 --> 16:31.080
You can sit in front of the cockpit.

16:31.372 --> 16:33.041
Oh, I wanna try going up there!

16:38.379 --> 16:39.923
This is awesome!

16:40.256 --> 16:43.384
The sea in Okinawa was great,
but this is entirely unique.

16:44.219 --> 16:45.303
It's truly beautiful.

16:49.807 --> 16:50.892
Cakey.

16:53.811 --> 16:55.772
Look at this clarity!

16:55.772 --> 16:58.525
If there were no waves,
you can see the bottom.

16:58.816 --> 17:01.945
Now I'm looking forward to
diving even more.

17:01.986 --> 17:02.987
Yeah.

17:03.321 --> 17:05.907
Have you researched the sea in Palau?

17:05.907 --> 17:07.408
A little bit.

17:07.825 --> 17:10.578
What I want to see
is the Barracuda tornado.

17:10.578 --> 17:12.372
Yeah, that's cool.

17:12.372 --> 17:13.748
They rise up like a wall.

17:13.748 --> 17:15.333
Or a school of trevally too.

17:15.333 --> 17:18.086
Ah, I saw pictures of those
before coming here.

17:18.086 --> 17:19.796
And we absolutely have to see...

17:20.088 --> 17:21.005
Manta rays.

17:21.005 --> 17:23.800
I want to see those giant creatures
with my own eyes.

17:23.800 --> 17:26.219
When you think about Palau,
it has to be manta rays.

17:26.511 --> 17:29.931
If so, then others might want to see...

17:30.098 --> 17:31.724
Hey, look over there.

17:40.149 --> 17:41.818
Wow!

17:41.943 --> 17:43.528
There are wild dolphins too?

17:43.528 --> 17:45.405
That's - that's so cool!

17:46.739 --> 17:48.783
You guys are really lucky.

17:48.783 --> 17:50.743
C-Careful not to lean out too much.

17:50.994 --> 17:51.786
Chisa.

17:51.786 --> 17:52.537
Yes.

17:52.537 --> 17:54.539
You don't need to be so stiff.

17:54.789 --> 17:55.790
But...

17:55.915 --> 17:57.709
A guide's job...

17:58.167 --> 18:00.587
is to ensure maximum safety...

18:00.587 --> 18:03.089
and provide a fun time.

18:04.299 --> 18:07.343
To do that, you have to
keep smiling yourself.

18:07.343 --> 18:08.219
Yes.

18:08.469 --> 18:10.763
I'm sorry, I'll keep that in mind.

18:10.763 --> 18:13.725
This is also the hardest part to do.

18:14.225 --> 18:16.769
In the end, guides are only human too.

18:22.900 --> 18:25.528
This diving spot is called
the Blue Corner.

18:25.737 --> 18:27.989
It's the most famous spot in Palau...

18:27.989 --> 18:29.532
so enjoy yourselves.

18:29.532 --> 18:30.700
Yes.

18:46.591 --> 18:48.384
What is this?

18:48.551 --> 18:51.179
So many fish
right after entering the water.

18:51.846 --> 18:52.889
Come to think of it,

18:53.097 --> 18:57.018
When I went diving as a kid, I was
overwhelmed and instantly loved it.

18:57.018 --> 18:58.269
Wow...

19:07.612 --> 19:08.863
I see.

19:12.867 --> 19:14.619
This view truly...

19:15.119 --> 19:17.497
could change your perspective on life.

19:23.586 --> 19:25.088
Good work out there.

19:25.088 --> 19:26.714
Good work, everyone.

19:27.298 --> 19:29.217
How was the sea in Palau?

19:29.217 --> 19:30.927
It was amazing.

19:31.010 --> 19:33.596
Didn't expect there to be
such a beautiful ocean.

19:33.596 --> 19:35.848
I'm so glad I learned to dive.

19:35.848 --> 19:37.558
Nothing better than hearing that.

19:40.353 --> 19:41.729
Did everything go alright?

19:41.771 --> 19:42.897
Yes, pretty smoothly.

19:43.398 --> 19:45.400
- Oh crap.
- What's wrong?

19:45.858 --> 19:48.986
I was so captivated that I forgot
to act like a bad customer.

19:48.986 --> 19:49.529
Ah.

19:49.737 --> 19:50.988
I forgot too.

19:51.447 --> 19:52.657
So they say.

19:53.574 --> 19:54.617
It's fine.

19:54.784 --> 19:57.537
Just watching how beginners act
when they're captivated...

19:57.537 --> 19:58.705
is a lesson in itself.

19:58.705 --> 19:59.330
Good job.

19:59.330 --> 20:01.582
There were quite a few moves
that made me sweat.

20:01.791 --> 20:02.667
Same here.

20:02.667 --> 20:04.669
That's good then.

20:04.877 --> 20:06.379
Is that really good?

20:07.004 --> 20:09.298
Diving three times must have
worn you out, yes?

20:09.465 --> 20:10.466
I am a bit tired.

20:10.591 --> 20:12.218
It is underwater, after all.

20:12.510 --> 20:14.804
But this really is
a fantastic part-time job.

20:14.804 --> 20:17.223
I didn't expect to be given
an experience like this.

20:17.223 --> 20:18.766
I'm so grateful to the boss.

20:18.975 --> 20:20.977
No, no, what are you guys talking about?

20:21.310 --> 20:23.271
The real work starts now.

20:23.438 --> 20:24.147
Huh?

20:25.064 --> 20:27.150
Enough playing customers.

20:27.275 --> 20:29.277
Hurry and take out the empty air tanks.

20:29.277 --> 20:31.487
Clean and maintain the equipment too.

20:31.487 --> 20:34.699
After that, prepare the gear
for tomorrow, and then clean up.

20:34.699 --> 20:36.617
Seriously?

20:40.496 --> 20:41.748
I'm exhausted.

20:41.748 --> 20:44.584
We had to get up very early
and then swim in the sea and all.

20:44.751 --> 20:47.879
Doing manual labor, cleaning up,
and prepping on top of that.

20:48.171 --> 20:50.214
Chisa, are you used to this stuff?

20:50.506 --> 20:51.758
Somewhat.

20:51.799 --> 20:52.008
MOTIVATION TO SMILE DAILY? OF COURSE, IT'S CHIS-- THE CUSTOMERS' SMILES.

20:52.008 --> 20:53.926
MOTIVATION TO SMILE DAILY? OF COURSE, IT'S CHIS-- THE CUSTOMERS' SMILES.
Nanaka-san is really amazing...

20:53.926 --> 20:56.179
MOTIVATION TO SMILE DAILY? OF COURSE, IT'S CHIS-- THE CUSTOMERS' SMILES.
if she's dong this everyday and can still keep smiling.

20:56.179 --> 20:57.054
if she's dong this everyday and can still keep smiling.

20:57.054 --> 20:58.097
Exactly.

20:58.097 --> 21:00.558
There must be days
when she's not feeling well, too.

21:02.226 --> 21:02.643
Yeah.

21:03.686 --> 21:07.356
So, to prepare for tomorrow,
let's have a light drink and go to sleep.

21:07.356 --> 21:08.274
Agreed.

21:08.274 --> 21:09.984
You're still going to drink?

21:12.403 --> 21:14.280
Well, good night then.

21:14.530 --> 21:15.406
Good night.

21:15.448 --> 21:16.949
Good night.

21:17.116 --> 21:17.950
Good night.

21:18.242 --> 21:19.994
I'll finish this and go to sleep too.

21:20.661 --> 21:23.498
Damn it,
they really don't broadcast anime here?

21:23.498 --> 21:25.124
Just like always, huh?

21:31.464 --> 21:34.133
You can take that thing off now.

21:34.133 --> 21:36.344
Ah, sorry, is it an eyesore?

21:36.469 --> 21:37.804
Again.

21:39.138 --> 21:42.183
Because I'm not used to it,
and it's big so it slips easily.

21:42.433 --> 21:43.810
Is that so?

21:44.185 --> 21:47.146
But if that's the case,
why are you wearing that thing?

21:49.607 --> 21:50.817
It's fine.

21:50.900 --> 21:52.443
I don't mind.

21:55.238 --> 21:58.866
The cold table surface feels so nice.

22:02.203 --> 22:03.329
Hey, Cakey.

22:03.704 --> 22:04.664
What is it?

22:04.664 --> 22:07.416
Sorry if I'm not getting this.

22:07.875 --> 22:10.545
Could it be...
you feel that way about Kitahara?

22:19.637 --> 22:21.264
3... 2... 1... Go!

22:30.815 --> 22:33.568
A sweet little love story!?

22:33.568 --> 22:36.320
Asymmetrical reflection in the mirror

22:36.320 --> 22:37.947
A shattered, crunchy heart

22:37.947 --> 22:39.991
Oh oh, stumbling around

22:40.575 --> 22:42.994
Oh oh, just acting on instinct

22:42.994 --> 22:46.956
Diving deep into my subconscious

22:46.956 --> 22:48.708
Tumbling and falling down

22:48.708 --> 22:51.294
A limit-breaking paradise

22:51.294 --> 22:52.545
Viva, cheers

22:52.545 --> 22:54.005
Everyone, cheers

22:54.005 --> 22:56.048
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:56.048 --> 22:56.757
Big trouble

22:56.757 --> 22:58.759
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:58.759 --> 22:59.594
Wa wa wa

22:59.594 --> 23:01.554
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

23:01.554 --> 23:02.263
Wa wa wa wa

23:02.263 --> 23:04.223
Let's go, everybody

23:04.223 --> 23:07.685
Dramatic just like a rainbow

23:07.685 --> 23:10.688
Your troubled smile
is absolutely priceless

23:10.688 --> 23:15.985
Total chaos
getting kissed by an octopus

23:15.985 --> 23:18.738
A mermaid washed up on the shore

23:18.738 --> 23:21.657
Darling drowned down
in the Dragon Palace

23:21.657 --> 23:26.954
The treasure box is just full of alcohol

23:26.954 --> 23:29.665
The ultimate license of our youth

23:29.665 --> 23:32.627
Find the treasure and checkmate

23:32.627 --> 23:37.840
An angel who overslept
from swimming too much

23:37.840 --> 23:39.300
Let's go, everybody

23:39.300 --> 23:40.676
Viva, cheers

23:40.676 --> 23:42.011
Oh yeah

23:42.011 --> 23:43.679
Viva, cheers
